{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.78,"content_digest":"4fd403f16af0975f815f153feb974a604f0196f180efeaa49f2e570d7e1eb6b9","created_at":"2026-08-23T05:17:15+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"3ad337762fd78710c677230355eca6b3f335ba1b535814544b2e88eb37730395","input_tokens":5815,"latency_ms":34833,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"b0b807ed2be367ce35e56be3eb33a48309617af58d12698a622717c0fbb4d239","output_tokens":2512,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:8936dd78a9d340025a63b750","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:underdetermination","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:physics:01M0PGSAVJXF930B39YZ5C9D15","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The claim is a specific instance of underdetermination: two distinct dynamical models (Cardassian matter-only and perfect fluid with p=(γ−1)ρ) are observationally indistinguishable for tests depending only on scale factor or Hubble factor, so those observations do not uniquely identify the underlying model.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T05:17:15+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.62,"content_digest":"d7b188635472a0a6464add94d0aa4982ff092fb861860307f0e3fb865dae11ff","created_at":"2026-08-22T20:42:36+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"c265aa38f47ccbe802f669fb2ba18c59415431697fc81deaeb47528f4639a23a","input_tokens":6134,"latency_ms":15357,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"b3c13b9ddc60c4402e0ded80f095fd5728279fd780eee0428bc956625ddc1763","output_tokens":2401,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:91a538557f7e82ab17887a76","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:human-factors","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0NKBKAR8DFY80M7SCHVW0R5","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle is a specific empirical instance of the human-factors meta-principle: it treats user trust in generative AI as part of a joint cognitive-technical system, dynamically negotiated through perceived task risk and communication mode, rather than as an external or static system property. The meta-principle's scope includes human-AI systems and user adaptation, which matches the principle's conditions of blind and low-vision users interacting with generative AI tools.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T20:42:36+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.68,"content_digest":"b13dab14292d09378b8bed864c69d99d9cd4f1808de51c4000cfdc64b98d3946","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:13:08+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"b5eee88c4bb1d10afd1d492ad7ea5e99cc60079c0da4ee26fea7acaa006c4dff","input_tokens":5570,"latency_ms":37317,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"e89ff6bcd728cfdde2e82e9573d401bf8423a8c6ebb200d431c4cec738432077","output_tokens":2414,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:957e1c27c1ee87eb4c3f6cf8","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:inductive-bias","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QC0MMKFVVZCDVXMRX5GD6E","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that data augmentation is a form of inductive bias and that generalization depends on matching that bias to the target environment. Cutout augmentation is a specific data-augmentation bias; the reported improvement in occlusion robustness is a concrete instance of such a bias favoring robustness to occluded inputs. The empirical claim therefore specializes the general inductive-bias principle without the meta-principle being sufficient to derive the empirical outcome.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:13:08+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.78,"content_digest":"e472922abaaecbbe2c453418636ff9ef2a03225b7540cf856a5ad754476be800","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:36:44+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:f8d4446845ff98a599d65de0","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:test-time-compute","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:general:01KZZYYDYAFE7CP4Y1ZH96Q8MB","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that allocating more inference-time computation through iterative refinement can improve answers when candidates can be generated, evaluated, or revised. The literature principle is a specific instance: chain-of-thought reasoning and self-reflection generate a corrected plan after code failure, which is iterative refinement under an inference-time budget.","relation_type":"generalizes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:36:44+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.78,"content_digest":"93d19a8e400e0bb1c61de6fe0ce58d0ca09ce3e16d993ab9060848150b0685a2","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:44:20+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:fad1dd2f766ebdcf4b8fdb69","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:measurement-validity","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:general:01M0AZY4ENRKB8S8GS8VB5QZV1","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The claim that activation-patching-based evaluation is more faithful and robust than output-level or white-box baselines is an instance of measurement validity: a metric is informative only if it tracks the intended construct with adequate reliability and invariance.","relation_type":"supports","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:44:20+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
